{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/623387-hedge-colonies","id":623387,"title":"Hedge Colonies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-11T09:45:05-07:00","id":623387,"title":"Hedge Colonies","content":"I was reading American history a few days ago and I noticed a lot of stuff about how our forefathers claimed the wilderness for themselves. The early colonists had to deal with dangerous weather, food and water supplies, and the occasional Indian war. This inspired the idea of the Hedge Colony, a vast Hollow formed by changelings either brave enough (or stupid enough) to form their own little state/nation right in the Hedge. One has to stop treating the Hedge as a barrier dimension and more like the American wilderness: free space for the taking, but dangerous to grab hold of. So what do you guys think of my idea? I mean I would have to figure out some kind of mechanic for this concept, but I'll do that later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T10:09:23-07:00","id":623420,"title":"","content":"I'll start by saying that I'm not a huge fan of C:tL. No real reason. I just never got into it.<br /> <br /> However, this idea sounds rather interesting. I kinda dig it.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for mechanics, have you thought of maybe using the basic rules for Woundgates from WoD: Mirrors? Yours seems like an idea leaning toward traversing mysterious ground, stumbling onto new and strange things, the pioneer experience but with MAGIC. That all sounds great.<br /> Woundgates, whether or not you call them that or use Mirrors, are a decent concept to get that feel while still keeping some (read: most) Changelings safely thinking your &quot;pioneers&quot; are cracked in the head for going INTO the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u201cNobody is purely good or purely evil. Mo</b></span><b>st of us are in-between. There are moths that explore the day and butterflies that play at night.\u201d </b><br /> - Suzy Kassem, Rise Up and Salute The Sun<br /> <b>(She/Her)</b></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/380-azraelfirestorm","name":"AzraelFirestorm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar380_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T10:24:12-07:00","id":623470,"title":"","content":"I have an entitlement in my sig - Chartered Kings of Nowhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-11T13:26:33-07:00","id":623618,"title":"","content":"I don't think Mirrors is necessary for rules about the Hedge, as the rules for the Hedge are already in existence and are far closer to the flavour of untamed wilderness than woundgates. A freehold in the Hedge needs to have a profound defense against Fae/Huntsmen/Goblins, as well as against madness. There are a couple canonical examples, one ending in mass fae invasion, the other from rapid clarity decline among the citizens. In your pioneer example, the Fae/Huntsmen would be hostile natives and enemy nations. The madness part would be the diseases faced. Protection from Fae would be relatively straightforward, keeping the Bulwark up and never letting it slip, ensuring your freehold's approaches include the human world (so that theyre safer in the Hedge). Sadly, to keep sane, the colonists need human contact and human normalcy. This part would probably be the hardest, and be part of the ongoing game and story arcs. its a mad world theyre living in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T12:04:34-07:00","id":624536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/623387-hedge-colonies?p=623470#post623470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an entitlement in my sig - Chartered Kings of Nowhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, your entitlement was an inspiration in a subconscious way, Kings Raven. BTW, I am a fan of your homebrew stuff. It is pretty good. But back to the topic at hand, I was wondering if some kind of land claim mechanic would be in order to make the Hedge safe. I remember a few years ago reading about how a Southeast Asian nation was hunting down these metal spikes left behind by a former enemy to defile their land. It gave me the idea of using some kind of Cold Iron spikes driven into the ground to kill off/stave the Hedge's influence on mortal minds. There is still a danger to Morality/Integrity just from being in the psycho-active Hedge, but the idea of free land up for the taking is just too good to resist for the courageous settler or changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T12:06:14-07:00","id":624538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/623387-hedge-colonies?p=623618#post623618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think Mirrors is necessary for rules about the Hedge, as the rules for the Hedge are already in existence and are far closer to the flavour of untamed wilderness than woundgates. A freehold in the Hedge needs to have a profound defense against Fae/Huntsmen/Goblins, as well as against madness. There are a couple canonical examples, one ending in mass fae invasion, the other from rapid clarity decline among the citizens. In your pioneer example, the Fae/Huntsmen would be hostile natives and enemy nations. The madness part would be the diseases faced. Protection from Fae would be relatively straightforward, keeping the Bulwark up and never letting it slip, ensuring your freehold's approaches include the human world (so that theyre safer in the Hedge). Sadly, to keep sane, the colonists need human contact and human normalcy. This part would probably be the hardest, and be part of the ongoing game and story arcs. its a mad world theyre living in.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know the lyrics to Mad World come to mind....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-12T18:02:19-07:00","id":624827,"title":"","content":"To answer everyone's questions, yes, there are rules for the 'taming' of the Hedge, in Rites of Spring, Chapter Four.<br /> <br /> THis is how we have settlements beyond stalls on the road side.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T03:07:35-07:00","id":625272,"title":"","content":"A similar idea a while back on this forum was refugees from disasters going to the hedge for refuge, so it was this idea from the opposite angle- Amerindians fleeing the estimated 95% casualty rates from the epidemics the Europeans brought, as an example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T07:32:38-07:00","id":626623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/623387-hedge-colonies?p=624827#post624827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To answer everyone's questions, yes, there are rules for the 'taming' of the Hedge, in Rites of Spring, Chapter Four.<br /> <br /> THis is how we have settlements beyond stalls on the road side.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, the answer I was looking for. Thank you, ArcaneArts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}